        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute and return the global min and max of an array and the corresponding lat-lon-depth locations . </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This algorithm works only for an input array that has a unique global max and min location. This is assured by introducing a factor that distinguishes the values of extrema at each processor.</para><para>Vectorized using maxloc() and minloc() intrinsic functions by <ulink url="mailto:Russell.Fiedler@csiro.au">Russell.Fiedler@csiro.au</ulink> (May 2005).</para><para>Modified by <ulink url="mailto:Zhi.Liang@noaa.gov">Zhi.Liang@noaa.gov</ulink> (July 2005)</para><para>Modified by <ulink url="mailto:Niki.Zadeh@noaa.gov">Niki.Zadeh@noaa.gov</ulink> (Feb. 2009) </para>        </detaileddescription>
